WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.257
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level C one.

2
00:00:05.557 --> 00:00:09.536
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.836 --> 00:00:17.422
Unit ten: Complex Passive Voice. Today you will report past beliefs with perfect and continuous passive infinitives.

4
00:00:17.722 --> 00:00:20.619
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.567 --> 00:00:25.032
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.883 --> 00:00:27.105
Is thought to have been.

7
00:00:28.117 --> 00:00:30.987
Is thought to have been means a passive about an earlier time.

8
00:00:31.583 --> 00:00:34.547
It is thought to have been built in 1200.

9
00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:37.663
Your turn. Say: Is thought to have been.

10
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:41.768
Is thought to have been.

11
00:00:42.517 --> 00:00:43.901
Is rumored to be.

12
00:00:44.917 --> 00:00:47.857
Is rumored to be means a passive that reports a rumour.

13
00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:49.927
He is rumoured to be leaving.

14
00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:53.622
Your turn. Say: Is rumored to be.

15
00:00:56.467 --> 00:00:57.758
Is rumored to be.

16
00:00:58.517 --> 00:01:00.180
Multi-layered passive.

17
00:01:01.183 --> 00:01:04.878
Multi-layered passive means a passive with several verb parts.

18
00:01:05.483 --> 00:01:07.262
A multi-layered passive.

19
00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:10.932
Your turn. Say: Multi-layered passive.

20
00:01:13.767 --> 00:01:15.580
Multi-layered passive.

21
00:01:16.317 --> 00:01:18.200
Passive with perfect infinitive.

22
00:01:19.217 --> 00:01:23.085
Passive with perfect infinitive means to have been + participle.

23
00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:24.870
To have been written.

24
00:01:25.483 --> 00:01:29.308
Your turn. Say: Passive with perfect infinitive.

25
00:01:32.167 --> 00:01:34.538
Passive with perfect infinitive.

26
00:01:35.283 --> 00:01:36.517
Reported belief.

27
00:01:37.517 --> 00:01:40.213
Reported belief means an opinion people hold.

28
00:01:40.817 --> 00:01:42.340
A reported belief.

29
00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:45.858
Your turn. Say: Reported belief.

30
00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:49.968
Reported belief.

31
00:01:50.717 --> 00:01:52.020
Layered structure.

32
00:01:53.017 --> 00:01:56.003
Layered structure means a structure with several parts.

33
00:01:56.617 --> 00:01:57.989
A layered structure.

34
00:01:58.583 --> 00:02:01.619
Your turn. Say: Layered structure.

35
00:02:04.467 --> 00:02:05.862
Layered structure.

36
00:02:06.617 --> 00:02:07.862
Formal register.

37
00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:11.802
Formal register means a serious style of language.

38
00:02:12.417 --> 00:02:13.859
A formal register.

39
00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:17.741
Your turn. Say: Formal register.

40
00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:21.810
Formal register.

41
00:02:22.550 --> 00:02:23.888
Objective claim.

42
00:02:24.883 --> 00:02:28.369
Objective claim means a claim presented without personal view.

43
00:02:28.983 --> 00:02:30.368
An objective claim.

44
00:02:30.983 --> 00:02:34.007
Your turn. Say: Objective claim.

45
00:02:36.867 --> 00:02:38.146
Objective claim.

46
00:02:38.933 --> 00:02:42.619
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:43.483 --> 00:02:48.757
Visal, how do historians say people believe the castle was built in 1200?

48
00:02:49.850 --> 00:03:04.948
The castle is believed to have been built in 1200. This is a complex passive: passive reporting verb plus a perfect passive infinitive, to have been built.

49
00:03:06.050 --> 00:03:08.502
What changes for ongoing actions?

50
00:03:09.617 --> 00:03:19.804
We use to be + -ing: The company is reported to be developing a new engine. The present infinitive shows the action is simultaneous with the report.

51
00:03:20.917 --> 00:03:22.661
How do we avoid confusion?

52
00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:36.021
Separate the layers: reporting verb in the passive, then the time reference. Is thought to be refers to now. Is thought to have been refers to earlier. Check which time you mean.

53
00:03:37.167 --> 00:03:38.737
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:39.583 --> 00:03:46.807
Grammar focus: Complex passive: subject plus is thought and rumoured plus to have been plus participle.

55
00:03:47.107 --> 00:03:48.329
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:49.017 --> 00:03:52.549
The castle is believed to have been built in 1200.

57
00:03:53.450 --> 00:03:56.262
The company is reported to be developing a new engine.

58
00:03:57.150 --> 00:03:59.428
The treasure is rumoured to have been hidden here.

59
00:04:00.367 --> 00:04:07.048
Use to be for now, to have been for before, and to be + -ing for ongoing actions. The reporting verb stays in the passive.

60
00:04:07.783 --> 00:04:12.328
Be careful! Don't say: It is thought to build in 1200.

61
00:04:14.267 --> 00:04:18.774
Say: It is thought to have been built in 1200.

62
00:04:19.074 --> 00:04:20.725
Use the perfect passive.

63
00:04:21.533 --> 00:04:24.337
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:25.133 --> 00:04:26.924
A Castle of Secrets.

65
00:04:27.224 --> 00:04:31.023
The castle is believed to have been built in 1200.

66
00:04:32.033 --> 00:04:34.869
The treasure is rumoured to have been hidden in its walls.

67
00:04:35.867 --> 00:04:38.133
The owner is said to be selling the estate.

68
00:04:39.133 --> 00:04:42.526
Each structure reports a belief without naming the believers.

69
00:04:43.533 --> 00:04:46.160
A historian must separate fact from rumour.

70
00:04:47.267 --> 00:04:51.303
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:55.810
The castle is believed blank built in 1200.

72
00:04:56.110 --> 00:04:59.926
A, to have been. B, to be. C, having been.

73
00:05:03.467 --> 00:05:05.466
The answer is A: to have been.

74
00:05:06.617 --> 00:05:08.767
He is said blank leaving the country.

75
00:05:09.067 --> 00:05:12.256
A, to be. B, to have. C, being.

76
00:05:15.800 --> 00:05:17.544
The answer is A: to be.

77
00:05:18.683 --> 00:05:20.683
To have been built refers to blank.

78
00:05:20.983 --> 00:05:24.706
A, the future. B, a habit. C, an earlier time.

79
00:05:28.267 --> 00:05:30.673
The answer is C: an earlier time.

80
00:05:31.817 --> 00:05:33.886
Which phrase reports a rumour?

81
00:05:34.186 --> 00:05:39.221
A, is sure to be. B, is rumored to be. C, is going to be.

82
00:05:42.767 --> 00:05:45.184
The answer is B: is rumored to be.

83
00:05:46.350 --> 00:05:49.615
According to the reading, where is the treasure rumoured to be?

84
00:05:49.915 --> 00:05:53.673
A, in the walls. B, in the garden. C, in the sea.

85
00:05:57.233 --> 00:05:59.407
The answer is A: in the walls.

86
00:06:00.600 --> 00:06:03.659
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:04.517 --> 00:06:08.560
Write a complex passive sentence about a historical fact or rumor.

88
00:06:17.350 --> 00:06:18.804
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:19.104 --> 00:06:32.812
The ancient temple is believed to have been built over several centuries. The architect is rumoured to have disappeared after finishing it. I use these passives to report claims without proving them.

90
00:06:33.112 --> 00:06:34.821
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:35.717 --> 00:06:43.547
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and complex passive: subject plus is thought and rumoured plus to have been plus participle.

92
00:06:43.847 --> 00:06:49.205
Today's value is intellectual humility. Admit what you do not know, and stay ready to learn.

93
00:06:49.505 --> 00:06:51.901
See you in Unit eleven. Goodbye!

94
00:06:52.201 --> 00:06:55.028
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

